PSSS — Particle Systems Screen Saver
====================================

This repository contains a modified and substantially extended version of PSSS.


The original work
-----------------

PSSS — Particle Systems Screen Saver — was created by Andreas Kardin, who
publishes as *mephzara*: the idea, the name, the mathematics and the original
implementation are his.

    Original source   https://github.com/mephzara/psss_js
    Original demo     http://mephzara.com/misc/psss_js/

`psss-original/` holds that JavaScript implementation VERBATIM: all ten files of
upstream commit 2934077 (18 September 2023, the current upstream tip), his own
README and licence copy included, with nothing added, removed or edited. Every
file in it is hash-identical to its upstream counterpart, and it is kept
read-only -- nothing in `psss-engine/` writes to it.

Between that original and the TypeScript rewrite there was an intermediate step:
further work was done here on the JavaScript version -- strange attractors,
preset breeding, a preview grid, preset import and export, and a control surface
-- which is what the rewrite's specifications were actually extracted from. That
intermediate version is NOT part of this repository, so that `psss-original/`
can mean exactly one thing. Nothing in it originates upstream beyond the
original it extends, and the upstream repository linked above remains the place
to find Andreas Kardin's own implementation.


Modifications
-------------

This version adds a second, independent implementation of PSSS in
`psss-engine/` — TypeScript and WebGL2 in place of JavaScript and a 2D canvas —
together with a preset library, a control surface, a Windows screensaver host
and the two reference documents in the repository root.

    Modifications copyright (C) 2025-2026 Rico Cozzio

The preset format of the original is preserved, so an original preset still
loads. `psss-original/` is frozen at upstream's bytes: nothing in
`psss-engine/` writes to it, and no further change is made to it.


